# Netlify. Both variants are the same index.html; the page reads /swe off the path.
#
# The trailing slash is stripped first, on purpose: at /swe the relative asset
# URLs in index.html resolve against the root (/assets/...), but at /swe/ they
# would resolve to /swe/assets/... and 404. So only the exact /swe is rewritten.
/swe/   /swe          301!
/swe    /index.html   200
